The graph shows $Q=200e^{-0.1t}$ grams of a decaying substance after $t$ days.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$t$ (days)}, ylabel={$Q$ (grams)}, xmin=0, xmax=27, ymin=0, ymax=230, xtick={5,10,15,20,25}, ytick={50,100,150,200}, samples=100, clip=false, ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:25] {200*exp(-0.1*x)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use the model to find the time at which $Q=50$ grams, correct to $2$ decimal places.
